# MotoQuant API — environment reference (copy to .env for local use; never commit secrets)
#
# EVERY variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set, `make api`
# (uvicorn motoquant.api:app) serves the full simulator, catalog, optimizer
# and leaderboard for local development.
# MotoQuant is free and open source (Apache-2.0): there is no billing,
# account or email configuration of any kind.
# Deployment walkthrough: docs/SELF_HOSTING.md

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the SQLite catalog. The repo ships a seeded motoquant.db, and the
# Docker image bakes it in; the website never writes to it.
# MOTOQUANT_DB=motoquant.db

# ── Chat assistant (POST /api/chat) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude only. Two assistants: the mechanic (Claude Sonnet 5.5, default) and
# the doctor (Claude Opus 5.5). The server's own key comes ONLY from this
# variable (on Render: the dashboard's Environment tab, never a file in git).
# Without it, visitors can still chat with their own key (sent per request in
# the X-Anthropic-Key header, never stored); keyless questions answer
# "assistant_unavailable".
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Per-IP units per rolling 24 h for questions answered on the server key: a
# mechanic question costs 1 unit, a doctor question 2. Questions asked with
# a visitor's own key skip this cap. 0 disables the cap.
# MOTOQUANT_CHAT_DAILY_LIMIT=200
# Trusted X-Forwarded-For hops for rate-limit keying. Unset = auto (1 on
# Render or behind a loopback/private-network proxy, else 0). See
# docs/SELF_HOSTING.md section 3g.
# MOTOQUANT_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=
# Agent web lookup: brave | serper (+ key). Without a key a DuckDuckGo HTML
# fallback is used; MOTOQUANT_WEB_TOOLS=0 turns web access off entirely.
# SEARCH_PROVIDER=
# SEARCH_API_KEY=
# MOTOQUANT_WEB_TOOLS=1

# ── Abuse fuses ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-IP rate limits on every compute-heavy route. Only disable for tests.
# MOTOQUANT_RATE_LIMIT=true

# ── Weather (live venue conditions) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# OPENWEATHERMAP_API_KEY=

# ── Observability (all opt-in) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sentry error tracking — a no-op unless SENTRY_DSN is set.
# SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# SENTRY_RELEASE=
# SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0.05
# SENTRY_SEND_PII=false
# Server-side usage telemetry forwarding to PostHog. OPT-IN: nothing is sent
# anywhere unless POSTHOG_API_KEY is set (events are otherwise logged locally).
# POSTHOG_API_KEY=
# POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com

# ── Free-tier hosting keep-warm (Render) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Self-ping so a sleeping free instance stays warm during the day. No-op unless
# RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL (set by Render) or this URL is present.
# MOTOQUANT_KEEPWARM_URL=
# MOTOQUANT_KEEPWARM_INTERVAL_S=420

# ── MCP server (motoquant-mcp) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOTOQUANT_API_URL=https://api.motoquant.in
# MOTOQUANT_MCP_LOCAL=0
# MOTOQUANT_MCP_TIMEOUT=90
